 ℓ))) A.goodState)"},"kind":"theorem","line":38,"note":"Gives the normalized good/bad decomposition, angle range, all-iteration sinusoidal state and phase-equivalent normalized good component when nonzero. It additionally states orthogonality and the successful-subspace equations. A zero-probability success branch has no conditional state.","open_assumptions":[],"premises":["0 < A.prob < 1; H is a complex inner-product space and A is a Preparation."],"reached":false,"relation":"stronger","review_binding":{"declaration":"QuarticQuery.Paper.quantum_grover_state","judgment_sha256":"b28cc1a3cd05f3e145a4c2343476679b180eefc816411b15a724385fc4d7b2ef","row_sha256":"b788afa651111ed8f78c31f090bc3cc0592f92c6c238c33a78e0fc5205bb17ee","schema":"quartic-tie-review-v1","source_snapshot_sha256":"0d109ea9e9b7f4a766640d406409e30589fb4c5a4e645b6d6888569fa2edf29f","statement_id":"claim-grover-state","statement_sha256":"724f2c145b2cb265ca10f926ea080eb120a4b6c69db9d311fd0e2090f4fb6ae7"},"review_evidence":"current","reviewed_by":"ai:round3-foundation-source-review","reviewed_relation":"stronger","reviewed_route":"same","route":"same","wrapper_comparison_evidence":"not_run"},{"build_evidence":"current","built":true,"compared":false,"comparison_credit":"none","comparison_evidence":"not_run","configured_checks":[],"declaration":"QuarticQuery.Paper.quantum_grover_zero","declaration_lines":[72,76],"file":"lean/QuarticQuery/Paper/QuantumAmplification.lean","hypotheses":[],"inspection":null,"kind":"theorem","line":74,"note":"Zero-success preparations have no successful component at any iteration.","open_assumptions":[],"premises":["A Preparation with success probability zero; arbitrary iteration count."],"reached":false,"relation":"unassessed","review_evidence":"legacy_unbound","reviewed_by":"ai:round2-construction-quantum-source-review","reviewed_relation":"partial","reviewed_route":"same","route":"unassessed","wrapper_comparison_evidence":"not_run"}],"ledger_history":{"added_in_review":false,"adjudication_findings":[{"claim":"State preservation sourced to BHMT Lemma 1 and Eq. 8.","id":"R2-C-BHMT","paper_locus":"Section 3.1","reason":"Read directly.","verdict":"accepted"}],"earlier_ledger_wording":null,"wording_changed":false},"original_statement_sha256":"724f2c145b2cb265ca10f926ea080eb120a4b6c69db9d311fd0e2090f4fb6ae7","passages":["upper-grover-geometry","CAT-claim-grover-state"],"review_scope":{"compared_text":"maintained_ledger_statement","leading_matches":[{"declaration":"QuarticQuery.Paper.quantum_grover_state","file":"lean/QuarticQuery/Paper/QuantumAmplification.lean"}],"relation_origin":"authored_review","semantic_examples":"none_indexed","type_and_axioms_origin":"compiled_lean_environment"},"section":"3.1","semantic_probes":[],"source_line":328,"statement":"For 0<p<1 write A|0>=sin(theta)|g>+cos(theta)|b>, 0<theta<pi/2, with g,b normalized in the successful and unsuccessful subspaces. After l Grover iterations the state is sin((2l+1)theta)|g>+cos((2l+1)theta)|b>. Hence measuring success yields |g> up to global phase, independently of l.","statement_sha256":"724f2c145b2cb265ca10f926ea080eb120a4b6c69db9d311fd0e2090f4fb6ae7"}
